    <string name="gs_tree_help_record">Values come from the authorised record. A tree number may be missing. Use the species and measurements to identify the tree in the field.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_diameter">Diameter is the recorded value in centimetres. Its method or class is not inferred from the value alone. A recorded class is displayed separately.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_height">Height entered in the record. Missing values remain unrecorded; no height is calculated here.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_recorded_accuracy">Accuracy reported when the point was recorded. It is separate from the phone’s current GPS accuracy. Missing, zero or invalid values are unknown. It does not guarantee the trunk location.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_guidance">Indicative direction and straight-line distance to the recorded point, with no route or access guidance. “Near the point” is a display cue at 5 m and does not guarantee arrival at the trunk. Identify the tree in the field.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_phone">Horizontal accuracy reported by the phone for a recent GPS fix. It is not combined with the recorded point accuracy and is not a guarantee.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_compass">The arrow requires a recent heading of medium or high quality, corrected from magnetic to true north and for screen rotation. Move away from metal objects. Low, unknown or old quality hides direction; a fresh GPS distance may remain available.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_gps">A position older than 15 s no longer supplies distance or direction. The last position remains a dated reference, never a current position. Search resumes with a usable fix. Permission, location service and reception are separate states.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_species">Counts of geolocated trees in the authorised context, before accuracy filtering. Counts do not depend on the visible map area and do not describe stand composition. Changing a species deletes no records.</string>
    <string name="gs_tree_help_filter">This filter uses recorded accuracy, from 3 to 100 m, sharing the Settings preference. Unknown accuracies are excluded when active. Records without coordinates are counted separately. It does not correct positions or guarantee reliability.</string>
